From: Eduardo Garcia-Madico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 17:35:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcn-bt-slim: stop pinning the SLIMBus controller awake

The probe held a runtime PM reference on the parent controller, and it
runs once per half of the chip -- interface device and ported device --
so it took two, and only dropped them in remove(). The module stays
loaded for the life of the system, so in practice the SLIMBus NGD never
suspended at all:

    qcom,slim-ngd.1   runtime_status        active
                      runtime_suspended_time   1885 ms   (68 min uptime)

Releasing both references makes it suspend immediately and stay there
(188888 ms suspended over the next 180 s), with the chip still
enumerating and reading registers normally afterwards.

It was never needed: qcom_slim_ngd_xfer_msg() already takes and drops a
runtime PM reference around every transfer, so the bus wakes up on its
own whenever it is spoken to.

Nor did it ever do what it was added for. Its own comment said so --
"this has NOT been shown to help: register access measured 0/10 both
with and without it" -- and it was kept anyway on the grounds that
holding the parent resumed was "correct regardless". It was not free:
it cost an always-on bus controller.

Note this does not fix the ADSP staying awake, which is what led here.
Measured: with the references dropped and the NGD suspended for three
minutes, the ADSP sleep count stayed at zero. This is a power fix on its
own merits, nothing more.
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c	2026-08-13 17:31:21.016466968 +0200
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcn-bt-slim.c	2026-08-13 17:31:21.059799881 +0200
@@ -26,7 +26,6 @@
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/soc-dai.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
-#include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 #include <linux/debugfs.h>
 
 /*
@@ -613,18 +612,6 @@
 	else
 		wcn_bt->pgd = sdev;
 
-	/*
-	 * Hold the controller awake, on the theory that its runtime suspend
-	 * drops the NGD's enumeration on the bus.
-	 *
-	 * Note this has NOT been shown to help: register access measured
-	 * 0/10 both with and without it. The one run that ever read
-	 * registers successfully (8/10) predates this call. Kept because
-	 * holding the parent resumed is correct regardless, but do not
-	 * mistake it for the fix.
-	 */
-	pm_runtime_get_sync(sdev->dev.parent);
-
 	dev_info(&sdev->dev, "bound %s (dev_index %u)\n",
 		 sdev->e_addr.dev_index == WCN_DEV_INDEX_IFD ? "interface device"
 							     : "ported device",
@@ -673,7 +660,6 @@
 static void wcn_bt_slim_remove(struct slim_device *sdev)
 {
 	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&wcn_bt->laddr_work);
-	pm_runtime_put(sdev->dev.parent);
 
 	mutex_lock(&wcn_bt_lock);
 	if (wcn_bt->ifd == sdev)
